\textbf{Case 1.3. }  $m_2\in[2/d,1/\sqrt d],s\in[\epsilon,s_0]$.
Note that in this case  $s_1=m_1+s\ge\epsilon,s_2=m_2+s\ge\epsilon$, thus it follows immediately from Lemma \ref{EpsilonTo1} that
\begin{align}
\begin{split}
\sum_{M_1,M_2=\frac2dn}^{n/\sqrt d}\sum_{S=\epsilon n}^{S_0}W(M_1,M_2,S)=o(1).
\end{split}
\end{align}
